id #uuid "125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-20959" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+3y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186640785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4b63c1c-5522-5b07-a23d-7c7d95d3734b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640548} {:answer/id #uuid "c064555d-7671-5a2b-8553-7970f952fd75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640576} {:answer/id #uuid "eb54230f-0e8f-5b6b-9b20-a8da607a3641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640626} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4d0da-724d-509e-b2c6-d40039895f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640637} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0ad112-4f45-59ed-90ec-3985d7c35847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4d0da-724d-509e-b2c6-d40039895f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640637} :answer-field/id #uuid "88b4fd01-fabf-5177-89d8-3602e8edba31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186640694}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9337e87-8282-59d9-8385-d5158f849042" :question/math-academy-id "q-20962" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2+y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f9f5b46-90ef-5f6c-b3c3-cb27660604fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3y+6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671746} {:answer/id #uuid "663701ee-ea16-5abe-b654-a4259844c1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3y-4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671748} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3179a7-f1b9-52b0-8b9d-a8413d704af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-3y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671754} {:answer/id #uuid "cd934be8-8701-5697-9a1c-e73f84ba0b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3y+4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671760} {:answer/id #uuid "f312ed05-3fd9-5f85-af4d-836d0af59e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6-3y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9f5b46-90ef-5f6c-b3c3-cb27660604fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3y+6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671746} :answer-field/id #uuid "58c80288-6831-57c6-9e8b-e1cc1634b787" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671743}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5eb285d8-9be0-5d20-a475-af1d186bdad2" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=6\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=6.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3y+6,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3y+6\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 3y+6 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨3y+6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce9dbfe-c27b-5acf-9e56-82d73066788d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2y+3,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671732} {:answer/id #uuid "56e51ede-6f53-57b5-bd4d-c469151cd54c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671742} {:answer/id #uuid "d7717cb4-ad5b-5fe5-88f7-1a9fa24d54a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2y-4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671762} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b48763-94e3-5ec2-9113-cbde07237195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4-2y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671763} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e704d1-f888-5868-b416-4111dda80b02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7717cb4-ad5b-5fe5-88f7-1a9fa24d54a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2y-4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671762} :answer-field/id #uuid "d303c353-e333-54ee-84c5-ccd298dcfdda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671761}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c9995c5-1dc2-5c84-888e-84f7f28ad60c" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2y-4,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2y-4\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2y-4 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨-2y-4,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e375b96-3cf4-5aa2-b2f2-5557565c83cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2y-6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671735} {:answer/id #uuid "33b84f36-89e8-5d3d-b3f1-611c33dbd2de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2y+6,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671736} {:answer/id #uuid "39378267-0a24-56f8-8087-d1e7ee4da02e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2y-12,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671737} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6d713d-931f-5d2a-8804-4b697d543021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2y-12,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671744} {:answer/id #uuid "b0244689-0a46-5853-9fec-f982a9fda63b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2y-3,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c6d713d-931f-5d2a-8804-4b697d543021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2y-12,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671744} :answer-field/id #uuid "86591107-a127-5d2e-9347-404b6dcfa373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671751}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c894149-7948-5b92-979d-5971289cdee0" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-12\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-12.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2y-12,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2y-12\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} -2y-12 \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨-2y-12,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a3a860b-e818-5fb7-a05e-97c8101d1c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671731} {:answer/id #uuid "3c87d3b5-b807-5fd1-a14c-5fe5f702fa45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671738} {:answer/id #uuid "4aec7793-7f3a-504b-adfb-3cdb19cb4064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671740} {:answer/id #uuid "65b9f15e-9dc2-57a7-8776-072fce7609ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671747} {:answer/id #uuid "6a555149-af22-5d1d-8b70-3429357ed0ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4aec7793-7f3a-504b-adfb-3cdb19cb4064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671740} :answer-field/id #uuid "9260ebac-0601-58c2-8fe2-3fe8f0a108e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671755}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8cc6b874-4ef9-5579-b3e1-061950bc9381" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 12 & -8 \\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671759 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2035e1bd-56b5-5578-8606-7fc651306db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2y-1,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671733} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6968fa-7e75-5f65-9340-b99eeb613b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2y+3,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671734} {:answer/id #uuid "452310bd-32d8-551b-9ee7-2345ff0deb23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671739} {:answer/id #uuid "bb158a33-be60-52fe-a0ac-971d43fe8f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671757} {:answer/id #uuid "c55f50f3-04c9-58f0-b74c-bf451a5462e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-2y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c55f50f3-04c9-58f0-b74c-bf451a5462e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-2y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671758} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e179302-8c5b-5fe2-bc46-441206b85088" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671741}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c89e5e36-218a-5433-9810-1b6f9389e970" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=2\\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-2y\\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix} 2-2y \\\\  y \\end{bmatrix}=⟨2-2y,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}]}
